;; bin/java-check's negative controls (doc/GATE-SURVEY.md, GTS81 (a), "As built: GTS72, GTS79-GTS82
;; (write-ahead)"): a run of one test, its subject, judged against another test's reference by the
;; level's own judge, which must say it does not pass. java.check/plan writes the reference's expected
;; results into the subject's plan (control lines: its first action's status and stdout digests, its
;; class files' digest); bin/java-check judges the subject's own run a second time against them, by
;; run_actions' judge (interp, compiled) and classes_verdict (classes), under the control's id; and
;; java.check/report (and bin/java-check --essential-compiled) fail the run when a control passes (the
;; judge passes what differs: 2026-10-31's two judges) or did not reach the judge while its subject ran.
;; No test of its own, no run of its own: the subject's run judged twice. The controls are no tests of
;; the records (check-LEVEL.edn), the classes, the essential list or levels-known.edn. The subject and
;; the reference: essential tests (their committed forms in test/java/forms/) that pass at every level
;; and whose JDK runs exit 0 with different stdout. :levels the levels it judges at. Read with the
;; Clojure reader.
